{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Bun's recap duplicates skip rows on large suites, causing valid substitution to be refused and the run to require human intervention."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A second skipped test with the same file and name is merged into the inherited identity, bypassing the check for newly introduced skips."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A baseline retained across a base update can cause a reintroduced skip to pass the inherited-skip check."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A credential in a baseline test name and a literal redaction placeholder in a different candidate name can collapse to the same identity and bypass the new-skip check."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The generic refusal message obscures the specific reason substitution was denied, making diagnosis harder without changing the decision."}]}